  "units": "cm",
  "description": "Interactive 3D figure for circular motion (ঘূর্ণন গতি), book page 36, topic 2.2. The book's three examples turn by themselves: a ceiling fan seen from below (বৈদ্যুতিক পাখা), the second hand of a wall clock (ঘড়ির কাঁটা) and the Moon going round the Earth (চাঁদ, nothing ties it to the Earth). Each shows the fixed point (নির্দিষ্ট বিন্দু), a dashed line to the moving point, and the circular path (বৃত্তাকার পথ) it traces. The dashed line says \"? cm\" until the student touches the moving point (or drags it round) to measure it; four measurements at different places give the same number (70 cm, 12 cm, about 3.84 lakh km): the distance is always the same. Speeds, and for the Moon sizes and distance, are stylised and say so. Test tab: 5 questions (find the fixed point among four, the distance after half a turn or one turn, what does not change, which everyday motion is circular, the Moon's kind of motion or its fixed point). Phone-first, Bangla.",
